{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774972367,"nonce":"U/qwHCG0t/OuySHFdSvC4t0teNQ=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM75KyAo","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/31","origin":"github"},"title":"Test thruster response and operator joystick control","message":"## Summary\n\nIncremental testing of the BizzyBoat control path from raw motor commands\nthrough to operator joystick control via the UDP bridge.\n\n## Control Path (from IzzyBoat reference)\n\nOperator: joy_node → joy_to_helm → Helm msg → UDP bridge\nRobot: UDP bridge → helm_manager → cmd_vel (TwistStamped) → echo_helm → mavros/rc/override → ArduPilot → thrusters\n\nKey nodes from `seafloor_echoboat_project11`: `echo_helm` (cmd_vel → RC overrides),\n`helm_manager` (piloting mode selection). Arming and mode switching handled\nautomatically by echo_helm on piloting mode transitions.\n\n## Steps\n\n### Step 1: Verify echo_helm + mavros control path on gabby\n- [ ] Run core_launch (mavros, UDP bridge) + echo_helm\n- [ ] Verify mavros connects to FCU and receives heartbeat\n- [ ] Check ARMING_CHECK parameter (IzzyBoat has it at 0)\n- [ ] Publish test TwistStamped to cmd_vel topic\n- [ ] Confirm echo_helm sends RC overrides to mavros\n- [ ] Verify thruster response (visual confirmation)\n\n### Step 2: Joystick on operator station (salmon)\n- [ ] Connect joystick to salmon\n- [ ] Run operator launch with joy_node + joy_to_helm\n- [ ] Verify joy messages publish and reach gabby via UDP bridge\n- [ ] Test piloting mode buttons (button 0=manual, 1=standby, 2=autonomous)\n\n### Step 3: End-to-end manual control\n- [ ] Joystick manual mode → helm_manager → echo_helm → mavros → thrusters\n- [ ] Test forward, reverse, turn left, turn right\n- [ ] Confirm standby mode stops all output and disarms\n\n## ArduPilot Modes\n\n- MANUAL: used for joystick control (echo_helm sets this on manual mode transition)\n- GUIDED: used for autonomous control\n- Arming/disarming handled by echo_helm via mavros/cmd/arming service\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Core launch running on gabby (mavros, UDP bridge)\n- echo_helm node available (from seafloor_echoboat_project11)\n- Operator bridge running on salmon\n- #26 (udev rules) — merged\n- FCU armed and safe to test\n\n## Safety\n\n⚠️ Thrusters will spin during testing. Ensure boat is either:\n- On a trailer with props clear, or\n- In the water with observers present\n\nPart of #14\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.6`","files":null}]}